        ("public_existing_scope_V1-transactional-kv", "Implement exactly apply_batch(snapshot, operations) in batch_store.py. This is a bounded transactional versioned key/value task. Modify only batch_store.py; do not change README.md or test_public_batch.py, create files, use network services or inspect outside this workspace.\n\nContract:\n- snapshot must be a built-in dict, with nonempty built-in str keys. Each cell must be a built-in dict with exactly keys value and version. A value is a built-in int (not bool) or built-in str. A version is a built-in int >=1 (not bool).\n- operations must be a built-in list. Each operation is a built-in dict: set has exactly op,key,expected,value; delete/check have exactly op,key,expected. op is a built-in str exactly one of set/delete/check. key is a nonempty built-in str. expected is None or a built-in int >=1, except delete requires the int. A set value has the same type rule as a snapshot value.\n- Apply in order to a staged copy. expected=None requires absence; an expected int requires presence at that exact current staged version. check only validates that condition. set creates version1 if absent, or increments the current version by1 if present. delete removes the key. Deleting then recreating starts at version1.\n- Any invalid type, shape, key, version, operation or failed condition raises ValueError. Do not return partial results. Never mutate snapshot, its cells, operations or their nested data on success OR error.\n- Return a fresh built-in dict with a separate fresh built-in cell dict for each resulting key; never reuse input cells. Dict order is irrelevant. Empty operations still returns a fresh copy. Calls have no retained state.\n- The module contains one ordinary top-level function with exactly the two required named parameters above: no annotations, defaults, decorators, classes, imports, global/nonlocal state or other top-level work. A module docstring and local nested helpers are permitted. Built-in operations only; no dynamic code, file/process/network/environment access. Keep the source <=65536 bytes.\n\nREADME.md gives the public regression recipe. These tests are partial, not the whole evaluation. Leave the implementation file and provide a concise final summary.\n\nStatic safety subset for the isolated evaluator: do not use reflection helpers (getattr, setattr, delattr, globals, locals, vars, dir, help, breakpoint), identifiers beginning __, private/dunder attributes, or attribute assignments. Ordinary type/isinstance tests, data-container indexing and public methods are permitted. This subset is an explicit task constraint, not an unadvertised grading preference.\n\nThe static name check is lexical over Python Name expressions, not only calls: do not reference or assign any of these names, even as harmless/shadowed local variables: __import__, breakpoint, compile, delattr, dir, eval, exec, getattr, globals, help, input, locals, open, print, setattr, vars. No Name expression may begin __. No attribute may begin _ or be assigned/deleted. These explicit restrictions apply in local helpers too.\n\nComplete static/export boundary: use the exact normal positional-or-keyword signature shown, with no positional-only slash, keyword-only parameters, *args or **kwargs. No async function, global declaration or nonlocal declaration is permitted anywhere, even unused. Imports/classes are prohibited everywhere. The implementation artifact must be a nonempty ordinary regular file, not a symlink or hard link. Isolated behavior checks use the approved Python 3.9 runtime, with 2 CPU seconds and 4 wall seconds per bounded test case.\n", .workspaceWrite),
        ("public_existing_scope_V2-stable-dependencies", "Implement exactly stable_ready_order(items, dependencies) in ready_order.py. Modify only ready_order.py; do not change README.md or test_public_ready.py, create extra files, access network services or inspect outside this workspace.\n\nContract:\n- items is a built-in list of unique, nonempty built-in str task IDs. dependencies is a built-in dict whose built-in str keys are exactly those IDs. Each value is a built-in list of distinct built-in str IDs from items. A self-edge is invalid.\n- Return a fresh built-in list containing every ID once. Repeatedly select the earliest ID in the ORIGINAL items list among all unfinished IDs whose dependencies are already finished. Newly ready IDs immediately compete by that original order; this is NOT alphabetical sorting or FIFO batching.\n- Reject any wrong type/shape, duplicate, missing/extra/unknown/self dependency, or directed cycle with ValueError. No partial result on a cycle. Empty items with an empty dict is valid. Dict insertion order is irrelevant.\n- Never mutate either input or any dependency list, on success OR error. No retained state.\n- One ordinary top-level function, exactly the two required named parameters above; no annotations/defaults/decorators/classes/imports/global/nonlocal state or other top-level work. A module docstring and local nested helpers are permitted. Built-in operations only; no dynamic code, file/process/network/environment access. Source <=65536 bytes.\n\nREADME.md gives the public regression recipe. These tests are partial, not the whole evaluation. Leave the implementation file and provide a concise final summary.\n\nStatic safety subset for the isolated evaluator: do not use reflection helpers (getattr, setattr, delattr, globals, locals, vars, dir, help, breakpoint), identifiers beginning __, private/dunder attributes, or attribute assignments. Ordinary type/isinstance tests, data-container indexing and public methods are permitted. This subset is an explicit task constraint, not an unadvertised grading preference.\n\nThe static name check is lexical over Python Name expressions, not only calls: do not reference or assign any of these names, even as harmless/shadowed local variables: __import__, breakpoint, compile, delattr, dir, eval, exec, getattr, globals, help, input, locals, open, print, setattr, vars. No Name expression may begin __. No attribute may begin _ or be assigned/deleted. These explicit restrictions apply in local helpers too.\n\nComplete static/export boundary: use the exact normal positional-or-keyword signature shown, with no positional-only slash, keyword-only parameters, *args or **kwargs. No async function, global declaration or nonlocal declaration is permitted anywhere, even unused. Imports/classes are prohibited everywhere. The implementation artifact must be a nonempty ordinary regular file, not a symlink or hard link. Isolated behavior checks use the approved Python 3.9 runtime, with 2 CPU seconds and 4 wall seconds per bounded test case.\n", .workspaceWrite),
